<title>USA: Bonneville offers no surplus power for Thursday.</title>
<headline>Bonneville offers no surplus power for Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) offered no surplus power for Thursday schedulings, marking the sixth consecutive day it has refrained from spot sales, the federal agency said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Before it withdrew from offering surplus power late last week, BPA offered up to 200 megawatts of firm power during heavy-load hours at $25.50 per megawatt hour (MWh) in the Northwest and $26.50 for COB/NOB deliveries.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
